{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And Amalek came, etc.</b> Scripture placed this passage next to this reading, to say: I am constantly among you and ready for all your needs — and you say, 'Is YHWH among us or not?' By your lives, the dog comes and bites you, and you cry out to Me, and you will know where I am! A parable: a man who set his son on his shoulders and went on the road. That son would see an object and say, 'Father, take this object and give it to me,' and he gives it to him — and a second, and a third. They met a certain man; that son said to him, 'Have you seen my father?' His father said to him: You do not know where I am? He threw him off him, and the dog came and bit him (Tanhuma Yitro)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:52:49.963290521Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}